@brief
A ticket, not an exercise.

    ORD-522  Orders must record when they were placed, and cancelling
             one more than 30 days after that must be refused with
             REFUND_WINDOW_EXPIRED.

Five buffers. Three change. Two are open so that you can check things
in them, and they must be left exactly as they are.

  1. order.entity.ts — `Order` gains `placedAt: Date;` directly under
     `customerId`.

  2. order.repository.ts — `toEntity` gains `placedAt: record.placedAt,`
     directly under `customerId: record.customerId,`. Careful: the word
     `customerId` appears earlier in that file too.

  3. order.provider.ts — two edits, far apart.

     In `create`, the values passed to the repository gain
     `placedAt: new Date(), ` inserted just before `status: 'PENDING'`.

     In `cancel`, after the `ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED` check and its
     closing brace, a blank line, then this block, then another blank
     line before the refund call:

         const days = (Date.now() - order.placedAt.getTime()) / 86_400_000;

         if (days > 30) {
           throw exception('REFUND_WINDOW_EXPIRED');
         }

  4. default.json — check that `REFUND_WINDOW_EXPIRED` exists. It does.

  5. registry.ts — nothing changes. It is a decoy.

Suggested order, because it is the order that makes the navigation
interesting: start in the provider on the `create` line and mark it,
write the `cancel` block, do the entity, do the repository, then
return to the mark for the last insert. Three graded files.

@keys
| `mA` `` `A `` | global mark, and back to it from any file |
| `g;` | back to the last change |
| `Ctrl-O` | back through the jumplist |
| `:b name` | switch buffer by partial name |
| `o` | open a line below and type |
| `:wqa` | write everything, quit |

@hints
`/status: 'P` lands on the `s` where the insert goes. Mark it globally
before you go anywhere.
--
For the `cancel` block, `/ALREADY` then `j` puts you on the closing
brace of the check. `o` from there, and type the block with its blank
lines; autoindent handles the depth, so type no leading spaces.
--
In the repository, search for `record.customerId` rather than
`customerId`, or you will land in `findByCustomer`.
--
Par assumes each line is typed once. About two hundred and eighty
keystrokes, most of them the `days` block.

@solution
One route.

**order.provider.ts** — `/status: 'P` Enter, `mA`. Then `/ALREADY`
Enter, `j`, `o`, and type:

    <Enter>
    const days = (Date.now() - order.placedAt.getTime()) / 86_400_000;<Enter>
    <Enter>
    if (days > 30) {<Enter>
    throw exception('REFUND_WINDOW_EXPIRED');<Enter>
    }

then Esc.

**order.entity.ts** — `:b entity`. `/customerId` Enter,
`oplacedAt: Date;` Esc.

**order.repository.ts** — `:b repo`. `/record.customerId` Enter,
`oplacedAt: record.placedAt,` Esc.

**order.provider.ts again** — `` `A ``. `iplacedAt: new Date(), ` Esc.

`:wqa`.

Every navigation key in this chapter had a turn. The global mark held
the one spot you knew you would need again before you knew how many
files you would visit first. `Ctrl-O` would have brought you back too,
six presses deep, and `g;` would have taken you to the `days` block
rather than the `create` line, because that was the last thing you
changed in the provider. Knowing which of the three you mean is the
skill; the keys are trivial once you do.

Two of the five buffers were never edited and one was never even
opened on screen. That is normal. A ticket touches the files it
touches, and the ones you open to check something should be left
exactly as you found them, which the grader confirmed.

If you found yourself typing `:b provider` and searching for the
`create` line again, that is the habit this chapter exists to
replace. It works. It is just slower than one key, every time, for
the rest of your career.

@start order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { CustomerProvider } from '../customer/customer.provider';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { EmailService } from '../../infrastructure/services/email.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(CustomerProvider) protected customerProvider: CustomerProvider,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(EmailService) protected emailService: EmailService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async findByCustomer(customerId: string) {
    await this.customerProvider.findOne(customerId);

    return this.orderRepository.findByCustomer({ customerId });
  }

  public async create(args: { customerId: string; total: number }) {
    const customer = await this.customerProvider.findOne(args.customerId);

    const order = await this.orderRepository.create({
      values: { customerId: customer.id, total: args.total, status: 'PENDING' },
    });

    await this.emailService.send({ orderId: order.id, template: 'order_confirmation' });

    return order;
  }

  public async ship(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status !== 'PENDING') {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_PENDING');
    }

    await this.orderRepository.update({ where: { id }, values: { status: 'SHIPPED' } });

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@expected order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { CustomerProvider } from '../customer/customer.provider';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { EmailService } from '../../infrastructure/services/email.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(CustomerProvider) protected customerProvider: CustomerProvider,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(EmailService) protected emailService: EmailService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async findByCustomer(customerId: string) {
    await this.customerProvider.findOne(customerId);

    return this.orderRepository.findByCustomer({ customerId });
  }

  public async create(args: { customerId: string; total: number }) {
    const customer = await this.customerProvider.findOne(args.customerId);

    const order = await this.orderRepository.create({
      values: { customerId: customer.id, total: args.total, placedAt: new Date(), status: 'PENDING' },
    });

    await this.emailService.send({ orderId: order.id, template: 'order_confirmation' });

    return order;
  }

  public async ship(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status !== 'PENDING') {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_PENDING');
    }

    await this.orderRepository.update({ where: { id }, values: { status: 'SHIPPED' } });

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    const days = (Date.now() - order.placedAt.getTime()) / 86_400_000;

    if (days > 30) {
      throw exception('REFUND_WINDOW_EXPIRED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }
}

@start order.entity.ts
export type Order = {
  id: string;
  customerId: string;
  status: OrderStatus;
  total: number;
  cancellationReason?: string;
};

export type OrderStatus = 'PENDING' | 'SHIPPED' | 'CANCELLED';

@expected order.entity.ts
export type Order = {
  id: string;
  customerId: string;
  placedAt: Date;
  status: OrderStatus;
  total: number;
  cancellationReason?: string;
};

export type OrderStatus = 'PENDING' | 'SHIPPED' | 'CANCELLED';

@start order.repository.ts
import { injectable } from 'tsyringe';
import { Order as OrderRecord } from '@prisma/client';
import { BaseRepository } from '../../infrastructure/base.repository';
import { Order } from './order.entity';

@injectable()
export class OrderRepository extends BaseRepository<OrderRecord, Order> {
  public async findByCustomer(args: { customerId: string }) {
    const records = await this.prisma.order.findMany({
      where: { customerId: args.customerId, deleted: null },
    });

    return records.map((record) => this.toEntity(record));
  }

  public toEntity(record: OrderRecord): Order {
    return {
      id: record.id,
      customerId: record.customerId,
      status: record.status,
      total: record.total,
      cancellationReason: record.cancellationReason ?? undefined,
    };
  }
}

@expected order.repository.ts
import { injectable } from 'tsyringe';
import { Order as OrderRecord } from '@prisma/client';
import { BaseRepository } from '../../infrastructure/base.repository';
import { Order } from './order.entity';

@injectable()
export class OrderRepository extends BaseRepository<OrderRecord, Order> {
  public async findByCustomer(args: { customerId: string }) {
    const records = await this.prisma.order.findMany({
      where: { customerId: args.customerId, deleted: null },
    });

    return records.map((record) => this.toEntity(record));
  }

  public toEntity(record: OrderRecord): Order {
    return {
      id: record.id,
      customerId: record.customerId,
      placedAt: record.placedAt,
      status: record.status,
      total: record.total,
      cancellationReason: record.cancellationReason ?? undefined,
    };
  }
}

@start registry.ts
import { container } from 'tsyringe';
import { OrderRepository } from '../domain/order/order.repository';
import { OrderProvider } from '../domain/order/order.provider';
import { OrderResolver } from '../domain/order/order.resolver';
import { CustomerRepository } from '../domain/customer/customer.repository';
import { CustomerProvider } from '../domain/customer/customer.provider';
import { PaymentService } from '../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { EmailService } from '../infrastructure/services/email.service';

container.register('OrderRepository', { useClass: OrderRepository });
container.register('CustomerRepository', { useClass: CustomerRepository });
container.register('OrderProvider', { useClass: OrderProvider });
container.register('CustomerProvider', { useClass: CustomerProvider });
container.register('PaymentService', { useClass: PaymentService });
container.register('EmailService', { useClass: EmailService });
container.register('OrderResolver', { useClass: OrderResolver });

@start default.json
{
  "ORDER_NOT_FOUND": { "statusCode": 404, "sentry": false },
  "ORDER_NOT_PENDING": { "statusCode": 409, "sentry": false },
  "ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED": { "statusCode": 409, "sentry": false },
  "REFUND_WINDOW_EXPIRED": { "statusCode": 409, "sentry": false },
  "CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND": { "statusCode": 404, "sentry": false },
  "REFUND_FAILED": { "statusCode": 502, "sentry": true }
}
